From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:05:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rda-combo: release the power token on every path

rda_wifi_bt_comp serialises the combo power sequences as a one-token
semaphore: init completes it once, and each wifi/bt power-on waits for it.
Only the success path gave the token back. A power-on that failed (an I2C
NAK, a failed table write) returned -1 still holding it, and every later
rda_wifi_power_on()/rda_bt_power_on() blocked for good, uninterruptibly.

Since patches 34 and 38 power the combo off, then wifi on, then bt on from
the I2C client probe, one failed wifi power-on (likely after a warm reboot,
with the chip still mid-session) hung the probe and with it the boot.

Move each power-on body into an inner function and take and give back the
token around it, whatever it returns.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor driver, not upstream]
